{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3100","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3100","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3100\",\"parent_revision\":\"cfdbae7d3facad7a4e9e5a0a08b3289e511efc03e33315e2aac5321213e73ab7\",\"root_revision\":\"cfdbae7d3facad7a4e9e5a0a08b3289e511efc03e33315e2aac5321213e73ab7\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: Ideas\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-21\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThis is an exploration/experiment item. The deliverable is an experiment result or design decision with evidence (a prototype on a real plan, a measured comparison, or a written design verdict) \u2014 not a mandate to ship the feature. Origin: comparison of graph-engineering research against the development-harness architecture, grounded against the #3060 agent over-orchestration incident (a task-worker recursively dispatched sub-teams after receiving orchestrator-voiced prose; ~$100 of unplanned spend). Shared design constraint across all seven exploration items in this set: the model keeps the judgment (scoring, declaring, deciding semantic dependencies) but writes it down ONCE, as typed data, at planning time; the mechanical consequence is applied deterministically by machinery that already exists (sam_schema models, DependencyGraph, the implement-feature dispatch loop, work-milestone). No new scheduler, no generic graph runtime \u2014 that larger direction is explicitly out of scope for these items.\\n\\nWhat/why: Dispatch capability is currently ambient \u2014 any agent with tool access can create teams and subagents \u2014 and an agent's role is inferred from the prose it happens to be handed. The #3060 incident showed the failure mode: a task-worker handed orchestrator-voiced skill text inferred a coordinating role and began dispatching its own teams and worktrees, even though nothing had assigned it that role. Separately, making role identification harness-portable is unresolved: the development-harness plugin targets Claude Code, Codex, and OpenCode, and the only verified role-detection mechanism (system prompt introspection) is Claude-Code-specific and unsanctioned.\\n\\nSub-dispatch is NOT inherently wrong \u2014 a subagent dispatching further subagents is a legitimate, recently-added capability and a good decomposition pattern WHEN planned. The defect is exclusively role self-assignment: taking the coordinating role without explicit assignment from the dispatcher.\\n\\nMitigates: role self-assignment / accidental recursive orchestration (the #3060 class); the unresolved cross-harness role-identification problem (role becomes data carried in the SAM plan, needing no harness runtime introspection at all).\\n\\nBenefit lands in: planning (the planner declares which nodes genuinely need planned sub-decomposition), every dispatch prompt (role stated explicitly from plan data), and the plugin's cross-harness portability story.\\n\\nProposed exploration: (1) add an executor field to the SAM task model with a closed enum \u2014 worker (default; performs the task, never dispatches) and manager (explicitly planned sub-decomposition; may dispatch within its declared scope); (2) swarm-task-planner assigns it at planning time; (3) the dispatch loop includes the assigned role explicitly in every dispatch prompt; (4) align the vocabulary with the role definitions being written into plugins/development-harness/CONTEXT.md (orchestrator = the single interactive agent acting on behalf of the human; manager/worker = agents acting on behalf of their dispatcher, role explicitly assigned); (5) verify the declaration survives round-trip into an actual dispatch prompt on a real plan.\\n\\nRelated: Item 3 (\\\"Explore declared per-task failure policies (retry/skip/escalate) including executor-loss\\\") \u2014 companion incident mitigation. Item 1 (\\\"Explore complexity scoring on SAM tasks to drive model tier, effort, and decomposition\\\") \u2014 same judgment-as-planning-time-data mechanism. The CONTEXT.md role-vocabulary work.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Experiment or design exploration executed as described (prototype on a real plan, measured comparison, or written design verdict)\\n- [ ] Decision recorded with evidence: adopt, adapt, or reject \u2014 with rationale\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **explore per-task executor-type declaration so dispatch capability is planned, never inferred** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: graph-engineering research comparison\\n- **Priority**: Ideas\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-21\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d7954e0aaf1d031f47b8130deaf75192ba6eaf9631d33a64d3cee8d94ca7e31d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQIpGBQ\"}"}